  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>stg_orders + customers (Stream Lookup) + products (Merge Join) + revenue and margin + the region key, to out/fact_sales.csv and the fact_sales table.</note>
      <xloc>144</xloc>
      <yloc>16</yloc>
      <width>896</width>
      <heigth>40</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>167</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>224</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>245</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
    <notepad>
      <note>build_fact - builds the sales fact from the three staging tables.
Runs after maintain_dim_region (it needs dim_region for the region key).

1. Read orders: stg_orders, sorted by product_id (the main stream).
2. Lookup customer: Stream Lookup on customer_id = stg_customers.id, returns customer_name and region_code.
3. Join products: Merge Join (INNER) on product_id = stg_products.id, brings product_name, category, cost. Both inputs are sorted by their SQL.
4. Customer and product found?: rows missing either go to out/rejected_unmatched_${SALES_DATE}.csv.
5. Revenue and margin (Formula, BigNumber 12,2):
   revenue = qty x unit_price x (1 - discount_pct / 100),
             rounded half-up to the cent with INT(x * 100 + 0.5) / 100
             (PDI 11's Formula step has no ROUND)
   gross_margin = revenue - qty x cost
6. Region key: Dimension Lookup/Update, lookup only, on dim_region (region_code = code, order_date between valid_from and valid_to), returns region_sk and region_name.
7. Fact columns: Select values sets the column order and precision 2.
8. Write fact_sales.csv to out/ (the file the accreditation check reads), then Load fact_sales into the table (truncated every run).
9. Count fact rows, written to the log.

Shipped data: 37 fact rows, 0 unmatched.</note>
      <xloc>144</xloc>
      <yloc>320</yloc>
      <width>1024</width>
      <heigth>332</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>179</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>225</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>251</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
